{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/1242478-help-me-plan-my-haltan-llinowan-war","id":1242478,"title":"Help me plan my Haltan Llinowan war!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2018-08-03T13:40:45-07:00","id":1242478,"title":"Help me plan my Haltan Llinowan war!","content":"For my next story arc, I plan on having the Bull of the North come back for a second round to add Llinowan and maybe Halta to his burgeoning empire. When planning an arc I try to figure out what will happen if the characters don't get involved and then let the players wreck my plot.<br /> <br /> This is my first exalted game and I have been running it for about eight months now but I have little knowledge of 1st and 2nd edition. It appears to me all things being equal the Haltans probably have a major advantage since the fall of the Tepet legions. However here are some things I am thinking about. <br /> <br /> 1) The Bull of the North can call upon his solar circle. Who is actually in his circle anymore? I dont know where to find this and use it.<br /> <br /> 2) The bull of the north has dragon blooded lieutenants. Where did he get these? How many does he have?<br /> <br /> 3) A variety of barbarian tribes are available to the bull as well. What tribes <br /> <br /> 4) The bull of the north has an entire empire he also has to keep protected. What can he really afford for more conquests to the south?<br /> <br /> 5) The Haltans also have access to various vassals like the Bloody river and a few other nations that escape my mind at the moment. Some like the bloody river even have three gods.<br /> <br /> 6) The Llinowans will likely want to call on their realm allies, but will they get much help? The Tepet are in bad straights and the impending civil war means that resources are unlikely to be sent to the edges. Maybe house Tepet needs to prove itself again to put itself back in the running. <br /> <br /> 7) There is the fair folk matter. Will they get involved? How so?<br /> <br /> 8) There is the matter of the two Gods. Caltia and Jostar i think. How will they intervene? <br /> <br /> 10) Finally, Chanta has two lunars. I wonder how they would be involved. Silver Python and Rain Deathflyer. <br /> <br /> What else am I missing in analyzing the resources these two nations might bring to bear? How might this play out? From my view at the moment, it looks like Llinowan is probably doomed in the long run. However Halta may not be willing to be as supportive as the Bull this time around. Anything else I should think about?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T01:27:47-07:00","id":1243147,"title":"","content":"1) The Bull can call upon the following: Samea (Important: Samea is a member of the so-called Persistent 20, she's the oldest sane Solar in Creation, and a known Solar-Circle sorceress with a history of calling on multiple Second Circle Demons at once. There is no reason to believe Samea could not call on a Third Circle Demon, if circumstances were sufficiently dire, or their goals particularly expansive. She also has significant ties with a variety of spirit courts) Raneth of Diamond Hearth: Twilight Caste, at least a Celestial Circle sorcerer, and a skilled Geomancer. Nalla Bloodaxe, Night Caste. Fear-Eater, Dawn Caste, Crimson Antler, Zenith Caste. Fear-Eater and Crimson Antler are both Icewalkers. <b>CoCD: North</b> (Sun and Ice, p.104+)<br /> <br /> 2) The Bull's Dragon Blooded are outcastes. He's killed most of the Terrestrials in the territories he's conquered. There aren't a lot of them. The one named, Mors Ialden, was really messed up by the last campaign emotionally.<br /> <br /> 3) When they say &quot;Icewalkers&quot; they mean all the tribes who previously did the nomadic, answer to the Animal Avatar deities. Yurgen and Samea pretty much have all these tribes, and they've overhauled them into a united military. Most of the old chiefs of the prior model of living have been supplanted by younger individuals more suited to the new order.<br /> <br /> 4) The Bull's holdings include Plenilune, the dominant of the five Saltspire cities, and another city-state that Nalla Bloodaxe was clever enough to suborn and become leader of without violence. Other than Samea's Manse-centric community, and these two locales, there aren't a lot of fixed holdings to keep secure.<br /> <br /> 5) CoCD: East details Halta's allied-states.<br /> <br /> 6) Honestly, this is just my own opinion, but I don't personally believe the Realm would meaningfully answer Linowan's call for aid with the Bull back on the offensive. Linowan isn't nearly as meaningful a holding as either Greyfalls or Port Calin, and with the Houses sort of jointly running the Realm, there'd need to be a consensus to mobilize a military response. How would that consensus be achieved, when every House is going to want the OTHER Houses to bear the burden of military assets deployed FAR from the seat of the Realm's power? Far more likely, IMHO, would be a token response and units sent to reconnoiter and determine the Bull's larger strategic goals. The Realm's interest would be in answering whether this is one more bite the Bull is taking, or is this move representative of a larger decision to move from the North into the East? Of course the Realm doesn't want an Anathema's powerbase to grow larger, but the same factors that have lead to the Wyld Hunt's drawdown creates the same throne-claiming-centric lens through which the Dynastic powers are currently viewing everything. If the Realm could stymie the Bull, without mobilizing legions, they'd jump at it...but no House is going to sacrifice their ambitions for the throne to &quot;do the right thing.&quot;<br /> <br /> 7) Halta's resident Fair Folk have often marched in exchange for first choice of battle captives. The Fair Folk would refuse to act as the &quot;tip of the spear&quot; but if Linowan shown signs of going down, they'll be the crows and wolves looking to feed on the wounded beast.<br /> <br /> 8) Jorst and Caltia were long of a similar/equal power level, but Halta came out of the war much better than Linowan did. They hate each other, and Caltia wants Jorst dead very badly. She fears being held accountable by Heaven if she tries to use her powers to eliminate him, but I could definitely envision the Eternal Huntress putting a finger on the scales to nudge her patronized nation back into the fray. Such influence would likely be subtle, and deniable.<br /> <br /> 9) Silver Python wants to step back and see if Halta can stand on its own. Rain Deathflyer, younger of the pair, isn't so ready to let go.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24378-wyldwraith","name":"Wyldwraith","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"111"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-06T08:56:31-07:00","id":1243220,"title":"","content":"Is this game 2nd ed or 3rd ed?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-07T13:47:36-07:00","id":1243591,"title":"","content":"3ed. It seems to me that llinowar is probably doomed. I suppose if the players intervene they might change things, but otherwise this looks like another nation to add to the bulls military force. Maybe a low level guerilla war would oppose the occupation.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3901-radiofreedeath","name":"RadioFreeDeath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"177"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T01:36:21-07:00","id":1243729,"title":"","content":"In 3rd ed, Samea probably isn't a Solar-Circle Sorcerer, and also she's missing an arm. She's been exalted for about 10 years.<br /> Also, Fear-Eater is dead, Tepet Arada killed him.<br /> <br /> Other than that, pretty much what Wyldwraith said, although since various stuff hasn't been mentioned in 3rd ed (Plenilune, a few of his Solars, etc) you could reduce his power if you wanted.<br /> <br /> Also, I don't get the impression he controls all the Ice-Walker tribes, just quite a few. It's not exactly easy to control nomads on a giant tundra if they'd rather just wander off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":2402,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","user":"The Wizard of Oz","date":". 08-08-2018, 05:37 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-08-08T02:28:36-07:00","id":1243736,"title":"","content":"I dunno if Halta would necessarily join in again.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Compass of Terrestrial Directions: The East</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Halta emerged on the winning side\u2014though many Haltans wonder what, exactly, they won.</div> </div> </div> </div>Halta suffered a lot in the war, and the only real consolation is that Linowan suffered more. Maybe they would be willing to join in again, but at the very least I think they'd try &amp; extract something from Kaneko in return. Of course, he never made any effort to shore up their alliance after the Battle of Futile Blood, so some Haltans wonder if he sees them as allies &quot;or merely a territory he is not yet ready to conquer.&quot;<br /> <br /> As far as the Lunars interfering, even if they decided that they were ready to cut Halta loose and see if it can stand on its own, a marauding Solar warlord is kind of beyond the scope of what the Thousand Streams River is supposed to be able to withstand. Why didn't they prevent Halta's involvement the first time? My read on it (and of course others may vary) is that they didn't expect it to be much more than the Wyld Hunt killing yet another Solar, therefore best to let that play out. To Halta, it would be little more than an especially memorable skirmish with the Realm. Now that the Bull of the North is a significant power looking to expand, possibly into Halta, they might be a bit more motivated to steer Halta away from him.<br /> <br /> Edit - Also I agree with WyldWraith re: the Realm's involvement. But I think that Sluluru's faction of Fair Folk might get a little more involved than just picking off the carrion.<br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Compass of Terrestrial Directions: The East</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Playing the part of Halta\u2019s valiant ally works very well for the Lord of the Lower Branches.</div> </div> </div> </div> But you could easily make either of the other two factions more prominent in your story if you didn't want the Fair Folk to be prominent.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":24421,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","user":"Katamari_Naneke","date":". 08-08-2018, 05:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/24421-katamari_naneke","name":"Katamari_Naneke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar24421_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2018"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"83"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}